// Test-bench input for ZoomInfo: {mode, ...params}. Pure sandbox -- writes
// NOTHING to Firestore, not wired into workflows 25/26 or site_outreach.
// Built 2026-08-03 after verifying every endpoint below with real PowerShell
// calls against the live API (100-credit trial), not from docs alone -- see
// testing_plan.md in Sales/zoominfo/ for the full verification log. Mirrors
// the search-then-enrich test bench pattern established in wf27 (PDL) and
// wf28 (UpLead), but ZoomInfo needs FOUR distinct modes instead of a simple
// search/reveal split, because ZoomInfo's credit model charges per-endpoint-
// type the first time a record is touched, then that record is free across
// every other enrich type for 12 months ("Under Management" -- confirmed
// empirically 2026-08-03: enriching a company then immediately pulling its
// Corporate Hierarchy charged only 1 total credit, not 2).
//
// FOUR MODES, mapped 1:1 to the four credit-relevant checkpoints in the real
// pipeline (testing_plan.md Phases 0-3):
//   "discover"        -- Search Companies (free, no cap needed on credits,
//                         only on result size for readability)
//   "enrich_company"   -- Enrich Company + Enrich Corporate Hierarchy
//                         chained together (1 credit for the company the
//                         FIRST time it's touched by either; free after)
//   "org_chart"        -- Enrich Org Chart (free once the company is Under
//                         Management from a prior enrich_company call;
//                         requires a real `department` value, NOT freeform --
//                         see Lookup Data /lookup/departments)
//   "enrich_contact"   -- Enrich Contact (1 credit per NEW contact record,
//                         independent of whether the company itself is
//                         Under Management -- confirmed empirically: the
//                         contact and company "Under Management" clocks
//                         are separate)
//
// This deliberate 4-mode split matches the real architecture decision
// already written into testing_plan.md Phase 4 ("Discover" free vs.
// "Enrich" paid must be two separate, explicit actions -- ZoomInfo can't
// use CoreClaw's always-enrich-everything pattern without blowing the
// credit budget in one click).
// FOUR MORE MODES added 2026-08-04 for Phase 0 free signal-scoring (testing_plan.md
// "intent and signals" ask) -- these are separate from the four credit-relevant modes
// above because none of Search Intent / Search Scoops / Search News / Find Similar
// Companies charge credits at all (confirmed per docs.zoominfo.com 2026-08-04: all four
// are free, though each returned record still counts against the account's Record Limit
// and each call against the Request Limit -- NOT the same thing as the 100-credit budget).
// Purpose: rank the ~289 already-discovered Ontario Airport companies (or discover more)
// by real signals BEFORE spending any of the ~35-40 enrich-company credits on them.
//   "search_intent"  -- Search Intent: which companies are actively researching topics
//                        like warehouse space / 3PL / flex industrial / cold storage.
//                        REQUIRES real topic strings from GET /lookup/intent-topics --
//                        not freeform text. Response shape NOT fully confirmed live yet:
//                        docs show attributes {audienceStrength, category, signalDate,
//                        signalScore, spikesInDateRange, topic, recommendedContacts[]}
//                        but no obvious top-level companyId/companyName field -- the
//                        response `id` looks like a composite
//                        "<hash>#<possibleCompanyId>#<date>" string. UNCONFIRMED how to
//                        match a signal back to one of our discovered place_cid rows --
//                        this is exactly what running this mode live should reveal.
//   "search_scoops"  -- Search Scoops: real trigger events (expansions, new leadership,
//                        funding). Accepts the SAME company geography/industry filters as
//                        discover mode (zipCode/radius/industryKeywords/etc), so this can
//                        be pointed at the same Ontario Airport zip+radius. Response
//                        attribute names NOT confirmed live yet (docs only describe them
//                        in prose) -- this mode returns the raw first result's keys
//                        alongside a best-effort mapping so real field names can be
//                        confirmed from an actual response.
//   "search_news"    -- Search News: real published articles, well-documented response
//                        shape (domain/title/url/pageDate/categories/description/company).
//                        IMPORTANT CAVEAT: this endpoint's request body only supports
//                        categories/url/date filters per docs -- there is NO company or
//                        location filter. It's a broad industry-news sweep, not a
//                        per-company lookup (that's the separate paid Enrich News
//                        endpoint). Useful for spotting named companies in the results,
//                        not for scoring our existing 289 rows directly.
//   "find_similar"   -- Find Similar Companies (Company Lookalikes): given one seed
//                        company (by companyId or companyName), returns up to 100
//                        similar companies -- widens the candidate POOL, doesn't score
//                        rows already in it. Different base path
//                        (gtm/copilot/v1, not gtm/data/v1) and a DIFFERENT OAuth scope
//                        (api:recommendations:read vs api:data:*) -- if this 403s, the
//                        ZoomInfo API credential probably needs that scope added.
//   "lookup"        -- GET /lookup/{fieldName}: generic controlled-value lookup
//                        (free). Use this FIRST to fetch real values for
//                        intent-topics / scoop-types / scoop-topics / news-categories
//                        before trusting freeform strings on the four modes above.
const b = $json.body || $json || {};
const mode = (b.mode || '').trim();
const VALID_MODES = ['discover', 'enrich_company', 'org_chart', 'enrich_contact', 'search_intent', 'search_scoops', 'search_news', 'find_similar', 'lookup'];
if (!VALID_MODES.includes(mode)) {
  throw new Error(`mode must be one of: ${VALID_MODES.join(', ')}. Got: "${mode}"`);
}

const out = { mode };

if (mode === 'discover') {
  // Free -- Search Companies. Cap page size for readability only, not cost
  // (Search Companies charges zero credits regardless of result count --
  // confirmed 2026-08-03: a live zip+radius test returned 183 real results
  // at zero credit cost).
  out.zip_code = (b.zip_code || '').trim();
  out.zip_code_radius_miles = [10, 25, 50, 100, 250].includes(parseInt(b.zip_code_radius_miles, 10))
    ? parseInt(b.zip_code_radius_miles, 10) : 25;
  out.employee_range_max = b.employee_range_max ? String(b.employee_range_max) : '';
  out.zoominfo_contacts_max = b.zoominfo_contacts_max ? String(b.zoominfo_contacts_max) : '';
  out.industry_keywords = (b.industry_keywords || '').trim();
  out.exclude_defunct = b.exclude_defunct !== false; // default true
  let pageSize = parseInt(b.page_size, 10);
  if (!Number.isFinite(pageSize) || pageSize < 1) pageSize = 25;
  if (pageSize > 100) pageSize = 100; // ZoomInfo's own hard max, not a cost cap
  out.page_size = pageSize;
  if (!out.zip_code && !out.industry_keywords) {
    throw new Error('discover mode needs at least zip_code or industry_keywords.');
  }
} else if (mode === 'enrich_company') {
  // Paid (1 credit first touch) -- Enrich Company, then Enrich Corporate
  // Hierarchy chained on the same matched companyId. Accepts companyId OR
  // companyName/companyWebsite (ZoomInfo will best-match on the latter, per
  // docs -- "the more details you provide the more likely we are to
  // provide the correct match").
  out.company_id = b.company_id ? String(b.company_id).trim() : '';
  out.company_name = (b.company_name || '').trim();
  out.company_website = (b.company_website || '').trim();
  if (!out.company_id && !out.company_name && !out.company_website) {
    throw new Error('enrich_company mode needs company_id, company_name, or company_website.');
  }
} else if (mode === 'org_chart') {
  // Free IF the company is already Under Management from a prior
  // enrich_company call on this companyId -- otherwise this is the FIRST
  // enrich touch on the record and WILL charge a credit. `department` must
  // be one of the real controlled values from GET /lookup/departments
  // (confirmed 2026-08-03): C-Suite, Finance, Human Resources, Sales,
  // Operations, Information Technology, Engineering & Technical, Marketing,
  // Legal, Medical & Health, Other. Comma-separate multiple.
  out.company_id = b.company_id ? String(b.company_id).trim() : '';
  out.department = (b.department || 'C-Suite,Operations').trim();
  if (!out.company_id) {
    throw new Error('org_chart mode needs company_id (from a prior discover or enrich_company call).');
  }
} else if (mode === 'enrich_contact') {
  // Paid (1 credit per NEW contact) -- Enrich Contact. Best practice per
  // ZoomInfo docs and this project's own established pattern (wf27's
  // search-then-reveal): get personId from a free org_chart call first,
  // only spend the credit on the ONE person actually worth revealing.
  out.person_id = b.person_id ? String(b.person_id).trim() : '';
  out.full_name = (b.full_name || '').trim();
  out.email_address = (b.email_address || '').trim();
  if (!out.person_id && !out.full_name && !out.email_address) {
    throw new Error('enrich_contact mode needs person_id (preferred, from a prior org_chart call), full_name, or email_address.');
  }
} else if (mode === 'search_intent') {
  // Free (Record/Request limits only, no credit cost) -- Search Intent.
  // `topics` MUST come from GET /data/v1/lookup/intent-topics -- check that
  // live first (same pattern as org_chart's `department` values from
  // GET /lookup/departments) and pass real topic strings here, e.g. topics
  // relevant to warehouse/3PL/flex industrial/cold storage searches.
  const topicsRaw = b.topics;
  out.topics = Array.isArray(topicsRaw) ? topicsRaw : (typeof topicsRaw === 'string' ? topicsRaw.split(',').map(t => t.trim()).filter(Boolean) : []);
  if (!out.topics.length) {
    throw new Error('search_intent mode needs at least 1 topic (up to 50) -- check GET /lookup/intent-topics for valid values.');
  }
  if (out.topics.length > 50) out.topics = out.topics.slice(0, 50);
  out.signal_score_min = b.signal_score_min != null ? parseInt(b.signal_score_min, 10) : undefined;
  out.signal_score_max = b.signal_score_max != null ? parseInt(b.signal_score_max, 10) : undefined;
  out.audience_strength_min = (b.audience_strength_min || '').trim();
  out.audience_strength_max = (b.audience_strength_max || '').trim();
  out.metro_region = (b.metro_region || '').trim();
  out.industry_codes = (b.industry_codes || '').trim();
  out.employee_count = (b.employee_count || '').trim();
  out.revenue = (b.revenue || '').trim();
  out.company_description = (b.company_description || '').trim();
  let intentPageSize = parseInt(b.page_size, 10);
  if (!Number.isFinite(intentPageSize) || intentPageSize < 1) intentPageSize = 25;
  if (intentPageSize > 100) intentPageSize = 100;
  out.page_size = intentPageSize;
} else if (mode === 'search_scoops') {
  // Free (Record/Request limits only) -- Search Scoops. Reuses the same
  // company geography/industry filter vocabulary as discover mode, so point
  // it at the same zip/radius/category used for the original Ontario
  // Airport discover run to find trigger-event companies in that same pool.
  out.zip_code = (b.zip_code || '').trim();
  out.zip_code_radius_miles = [10, 25, 50, 100, 250].includes(parseInt(b.zip_code_radius_miles, 10))
    ? parseInt(b.zip_code_radius_miles, 10) : 25;
  out.employee_range_max = b.employee_range_max ? String(b.employee_range_max) : '';
  out.zoominfo_contacts_max = b.zoominfo_contacts_max ? String(b.zoominfo_contacts_max) : '';
  out.industry_keywords = (b.industry_keywords || '').trim();
  // scoop_types / scoop_topics should come from GET /lookup/scoop-types and
  // GET /lookup/scoop-topics -- check those live first, same as intent-topics.
  out.scoop_types = (b.scoop_types || '').trim();
  out.scoop_topics = (b.scoop_topics || '').trim();
  out.published_start_date = (b.published_start_date || '').trim();
  out.published_end_date = (b.published_end_date || '').trim();
  let scoopPageSize = parseInt(b.page_size, 10);
  if (!Number.isFinite(scoopPageSize) || scoopPageSize < 1) scoopPageSize = 25;
  if (scoopPageSize > 100) scoopPageSize = 100;
  out.page_size = scoopPageSize;
  if (!out.zip_code && !out.industry_keywords && !out.scoop_types && !out.scoop_topics) {
    throw new Error('search_scoops mode needs at least one filter: zip_code, industry_keywords, scoop_types, or scoop_topics.');
  }
} else if (mode === 'search_news') {
  // Free (Record/Request limits only) -- Search News. NOT a per-company
  // lookup -- only categories/url/date filters exist on this endpoint (see
  // comment block above). categories should come from
  // GET /lookup/news-categories.
  const catsRaw = b.categories;
  out.categories = Array.isArray(catsRaw) ? catsRaw : (typeof catsRaw === 'string' ? catsRaw.split(',').map(c => c.trim()).filter(Boolean) : []);
  out.page_date_min = (b.page_date_min || '').trim();
  out.page_date_max = (b.page_date_max || '').trim();
  const urlRaw = b.url;
  out.url = Array.isArray(urlRaw) ? urlRaw : (typeof urlRaw === 'string' && urlRaw ? [urlRaw] : []);
  let newsPageSize = parseInt(b.page_size, 10);
  if (!Number.isFinite(newsPageSize) || newsPageSize < 1) newsPageSize = 25;
  if (newsPageSize > 100) newsPageSize = 100;
  out.page_size = newsPageSize;
  if (!out.categories.length && !out.page_date_min && !out.page_date_max && !out.url.length) {
    throw new Error('search_news mode needs at least one of: categories, page_date_min/page_date_max, or url.');
  }
} else if (mode === 'find_similar') {
  // Free -- Company Lookalikes (GET, different base path gtm/copilot/v1 and
  // a different OAuth scope, api:recommendations:read -- see comment block
  // above). Give it ONE seed company you already know is a good fit (e.g.
  // an existing tenant or an ecommerce_brand_pilot account) to widen the
  // candidate pool, not to score companies already discovered.
  out.company_id = b.company_id ? String(b.company_id).trim() : '';
  out.company_name = (b.company_name || '').trim();
  if (!out.company_id && !out.company_name) {
    throw new Error('find_similar mode needs company_id or company_name (the seed company to find lookalikes for).');
  }
} else if (mode === 'lookup') {
  // Free -- GET /gtm/data/v1/lookup/{fieldName}. Added 2026-08-04 to check
  // controlled values (intent-topics, scoop-types, scoop-topics,
  // news-categories, departments, etc.) before trusting freeform-looking
  // inputs on search_intent/search_scoops/search_news.
  out.field = (b.field || '').trim();
  if (!out.field) {
    throw new Error("lookup mode needs field, e.g. 'intent-topics', 'scoop-types', 'scoop-topics', 'news-categories', or 'departments'.");
  }
} else if (mode === 'discover' || mode === 'enrich_company' || mode === 'org_chart' || mode === 'enrich_contact') {
  // handled above, nothing more to do here -- this branch only exists so the
  // final else below stays reachable for truly-unknown modes despite the
  // VALID_MODES check already having caught them earlier.
}

return [{ json: out }];

// Real request shape confirmed via docs.zoominfo.com OpenAPI spec
// (searchinterface_searchcompany) 2026-08-03: POST body is
// {data:{type:"CompanySearch", attributes:{...filters}}}, page[number]/
// page[size]/sort are URL query params, NOT body fields. Free endpoint --
// no credit cost regardless of result count or page size.
const ctx = $json;
const attrs = {};
if (ctx.zip_code) {
  attrs.zipCode = ctx.zip_code;
  attrs.zipCodeRadiusMiles = ctx.zip_code_radius_miles;
}
if (ctx.employee_range_max) attrs.employeeRangeMax = ctx.employee_range_max;
if (ctx.zoominfo_contacts_max) attrs.zoominfoContactsMax = ctx.zoominfo_contacts_max;
if (ctx.industry_keywords) attrs.industryKeywords = ctx.industry_keywords;
attrs.excludeDefunctCompanies = ctx.exclude_defunct;
return [{ json: {
  ...ctx,
  requestBody: { data: { type: 'CompanySearch', attributes: attrs } }
} }];

// Shapes the discover-mode response. Search Companies only returns basic
// fields (name, city, state, website, logo, managementStatus) per real
// verified response shape -- full firmographics/hierarchy need a separate
// enrich_company call on whichever companyId looks worth spending a credit
// on. Nothing written to Firestore.
//
// PARSING QUIRK (found 2026-08-03 live in n8n): ZoomInfo returns
// Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json, which n8n's HTTP Request node
// autodetect does NOT recognize as JSON -- it comes through as
// {data: "<the whole real response as a JSON string>"} instead of a
// parsed object. parseResp() below unwraps that case; if a node's Response
// Format is ever explicitly set to JSON, raw.data will already be an
// array/object and parseResp() is a no-op.
function parseResp(raw) {
  if (raw && typeof raw.data === 'string') {
    try { return JSON.parse(raw.data); } catch (e) { return raw; }
  }
  return raw;
}
const resp = parseResp($json || {});
const rows = Array.isArray(resp.data) ? resp.data : [];
const candidates = rows.map(r => ({
  company_id: r.id || null,
  name: r.attributes ? (r.attributes.name || null) : null,
  city: r.attributes ? (r.attributes.city || null) : null,
  state: r.attributes ? (r.attributes.state || null) : null,
  website: r.attributes ? (r.attributes.website || null) : null,
  under_management: r.attributes && r.attributes.managementStatus ? !!r.attributes.managementStatus.underManagement : false
}));
return [{ json: {
  provider: 'zoominfo',
  mode: 'discover',
  total_results: resp.meta && resp.meta.totalResults ? resp.meta.totalResults : candidates.length,
  candidates_returned: candidates.length,
  candidates,
  credits_spent: 0,
  note: candidates.length === 0 ? 'No matches -- widen zip_code_radius_miles or drop zoominfo_contacts_max.' : 'Free search only. Pick a company_id worth spending a credit on and call mode=enrich_company next.'
} }];

// Real request shape confirmed via docs.zoominfo.com OpenAPI spec
// (enrichinterface_enrichcompany) 2026-08-03: {data:{type:"CompanyEnrich",
// attributes:{matchCompanyInput:[{companyId|companyName|companyWebsite}],
// outputFields:[...]}}}. matchCompanyInput.companyId is an INTEGER, not a
// string -- confirmed against the real schema, cast explicitly below.
// outputFields chosen from the real Lookup Enrich Fields (entity=company)
// results verified 2026-08-03, all accessGranted:true on this account.
const ctx = $json;
const input = {};
if (ctx.company_id) input.companyId = parseInt(ctx.company_id, 10);
if (ctx.company_name) input.companyName = ctx.company_name;
if (ctx.company_website) input.companyWebsite = ctx.company_website;
const outputFields = [
  'id', 'name', 'website', 'phone', 'street', 'city', 'state', 'zipCode', 'country',
  'employeeCount', 'revenue', 'primaryIndustry', 'subUnitType',
  'parentId', 'parentName', 'ultimateParentId', 'ultimateParentName',
  'numberOfContactsInZoomInfo'
];
return [{ json: {
  ...ctx,
  requestBody: { data: { type: 'CompanyEnrich', attributes: { matchCompanyInput: [input], outputFields } } }
} }];

// Pulls the matched companyId out of the Enrich Company result so the
// chained Corporate Hierarchy call always uses ZoomInfo's real matched ID
// -- not whatever the caller originally passed in (which might have been a
// companyName/companyWebsite guess that ZoomInfo best-matched to a
// different id). If Enrich Company came back NO_MATCH, skip straight to
// building an error response instead of chaining a hierarchy call for a
// company that doesn't exist.
//
// PARSING QUIRK (found 2026-08-03 live in n8n): ZoomInfo's
// application/vnd.api+json Content-Type isn't autodetected as JSON by
// n8n's HTTP Request node, so the real response can arrive as
// {data: "<json string>"} instead of a parsed object. Unwrap that here.
function parseResp(raw) {
  if (raw && typeof raw.data === 'string') {
    try { return JSON.parse(raw.data); } catch (e) { return raw; }
  }
  return raw;
}
const enrichResp = parseResp($json || {});
const row = Array.isArray(enrichResp.data) ? enrichResp.data[0] : null;
const matchStatus = row && row.meta ? row.meta.matchStatus : (enrichResp.errors ? 'ERROR' : 'NO_MATCH');
// BUG FIX 2026-08-03: ZoomInfo's JSON:API responses put `id` at the TOP
// LEVEL of the resource object (row.id), never inside row.attributes.
// Reading row.attributes.id silently returned null even on a real
// FULL_MATCH, which broke this chained Corporate Hierarchy call (sent
// companyId: NaN) without throwing any visible error -- the resulting
// null familyTree/parentage looked like "no hierarchy data" instead of
// "broken request".
const matchedCompanyId = row ? row.id : null;
return [{ json: {
  enrich_company_raw: enrichResp,
  match_status: matchStatus,
  matched_company_id: matchedCompanyId,
  requestBody: matchedCompanyId ? {
    data: {
      type: 'CorporateHierarchyEnrich',
      attributes: {
        matchCompanyInput: [{ companyId: parseInt(matchedCompanyId, 10) }],
        outputFields: ['companyId', 'familyTree', 'parentage']
      }
    }
  } : null
} }];

// Merges Enrich Company + Enrich Corporate Hierarchy into one response.
// Real-world proof this matters (2026-08-03 live test): DSI Logistics
// looked like a perfect small-business target by employeeCount alone, but
// came back subUnitType "Acquisition" under ultimateParentName "AP Moller
// Group" (Maersk's parent) -- exactly the trap this hierarchy step exists
// to catch before wasting an outreach touch on someone with no signing
// authority. Both calls together should total 1 credit on a first touch
// (confirmed empirically), 0 on any company already Under Management.
function parseResp(raw) {
  if (raw && typeof raw.data === 'string') {
    try { return JSON.parse(raw.data); } catch (e) { return raw; }
  }
  return raw;
}
const prev = $('Extract matched companyId').first().json;
const enrichRow = Array.isArray(prev.enrich_company_raw.data) ? prev.enrich_company_raw.data[0] : null;
const a = enrichRow ? (enrichRow.attributes || {}) : {};
const hierarchyResp = parseResp($json || {});
const hierarchyRow = Array.isArray(hierarchyResp.data) ? hierarchyResp.data[0] : null;
const hAttrs = hierarchyRow && hierarchyRow.type === 'CorporateHierarchy' ? (hierarchyRow.attributes || {}) : null;
return [{ json: {
  provider: 'zoominfo',
  mode: 'enrich_company',
  match_status: prev.match_status,
  company_id: prev.matched_company_id,
  name: a.name || null,
  website: a.website || null,
  phone: a.phone || null,
  address: { street: a.street || null, city: a.city || null, state: a.state || null, zipCode: a.zipCode || null, country: a.country || null },
  employee_count: a.employeeCount || null,
  revenue: a.revenue || null,
  primary_industry: a.primaryIndustry || null,
  sub_unit_type: a.subUnitType || null,
  parent_name: a.parentName || null,
  ultimate_parent_name: a.ultimateParentName || null,
  // subUnitType "Unspecified" is one of ZoomInfo's own real enum values
  // (alongside Location/Division/Acquisition/Subsidiary/FormerNewName) and
  // MEANS "no hierarchy classification on file" -- not "flagged as a
  // sub-unit". Confirmed live 2026-08-03: Coast Fulfillment came back with
  // subUnitType "Unspecified" and both parent fields null, i.e. genuinely
  // no parent signal, not a subsidiary. Only treat it as a real flag when
  // subUnitType is a meaningful non-Unspecified value OR a parent name is
  // actually populated.
  is_independent: !(a.parentName || a.ultimateParentName) && !(a.subUnitType && a.subUnitType !== 'Unspecified'),
  corporate_family_tree: hAttrs ? (hAttrs.familyTree || null) : null,
  corporate_parentage: hAttrs ? (hAttrs.parentage || null) : null,
  note: prev.match_status !== 'FULL_MATCH' ? `Enrich Company match status was ${prev.match_status} -- no credit charged, but no usable data either.` : ((a.parentName || a.ultimateParentName) || (a.subUnitType && a.subUnitType !== 'Unspecified') ? `Flagged as ${a.subUnitType || 'a sub-unit'} under ${a.ultimateParentName || a.parentName} -- check who actually has signing authority before running org_chart.` : 'No parent flagged -- looks independent, likely has local signing authority.')
} }];

// Real request shape confirmed via docs.zoominfo.com OpenAPI spec
// (enrichinterface_enrichorgchart) 2026-08-03: {data:{type:"OrgChartEnrich",
// attributes:{companyId:"<string>", department:"<comma-separated string>"}}}
// Note companyId is a STRING here (unlike Enrich Company/Corporate
// Hierarchy where it's an integer) -- confirmed against the real schema,
// don't cast it. `department` values are a controlled list from
// GET /lookup/departments, live-verified 2026-08-03.
const ctx = $json;
return [{ json: {
  ...ctx,
  requestBody: {
    data: {
      type: 'OrgChartEnrich',
      attributes: { companyId: String(ctx.company_id), department: ctx.department }
    }
  }
} }];

// Shapes the org_chart response. Real verified response (2026-08-03, live
// test on DSI Logistics/Operations dept) returned 24 contacts with
// firstName/lastName/title/department/jobFunction/orgChartTier/
// orgChartSubTier/hasDirectPhone -- but NOT hasEmail, even though the
// schema documents it. Don't assume hasEmail will be populated; sort
// candidates by orgChartTier ascending (1 = most senior) to surface the
// best decision-maker first. Free once the company is Under Management --
// if this is the FIRST touch on the company, it charges 1 credit instead,
// same rule as any other enrich endpoint.
//
// PARSING QUIRK (found 2026-08-03 live in n8n): ZoomInfo's
// application/vnd.api+json Content-Type isn't autodetected as JSON by
// n8n's HTTP Request node, so the real response can arrive as
// {data: "<json string>"} instead of a parsed object. Unwrap that here.
function parseResp(raw) {
  if (raw && typeof raw.data === 'string') {
    try { return JSON.parse(raw.data); } catch (e) { return raw; }
  }
  return raw;
}
